WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.770
For decades, a familiar checkbox has asked

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.810
us to prove that we are human.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.729
METTLE approaches the encounter from another
direction,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.809
by offering challenges designed around
machine capabilities

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.690
and observing how a respondent performs.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.129
That shift opens an interesting experimental
question:

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.790
what can a carefully bounded interaction
tell

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.629
us about the behaviour of the system

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.250
answering?

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.450
The useful starting point is a measurement

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.249
made in a particular session.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.329
METTLE stands for Machine Evaluation Through
Turing-inverse

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.390
Logic Examination.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.210
Its experimental protocol places each
session under

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.550
a named, versioned policy, so the challenge,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.910
the response and the interpretation belong
to

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.749
an explicit frame of reference.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.229
The server records answers, timing and
scores,

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.630
creating a record that another party can

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.230
examine.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.070
This gives a result a precise meaning:

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.230
it describes observed behaviour under the
conditions

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.268
of that session.

00:01:09.137 --> 00:01:12.577
The quick API offers a compact screening,

00:01:12.977 --> 00:01:15.577
including an arithmetic challenge that asks
for

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:17.816
the sum, difference or product of two

00:01:18.057 --> 00:01:20.296
eight-digit numbers within half a second.

00:01:21.257 --> 00:01:23.977
Other tasks ask the respondent to continue

00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:27.376
a generated token sequence or satisfy an

00:01:27.457 --> 00:01:28.937
exact formatting rule.

00:01:29.937 --> 00:01:34.217
Further challenges examine consistency,
self-description and changes

00:01:34.377 --> 00:01:35.176
after feedback.

00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:39.196
These are observable response patterns, and
they

00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:42.437
can be produced by people, models,
purpose-built

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:44.517
solvers or relayed answers.

00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:47.976
Their interpretation therefore calls for
care.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:53.870
The separate authenticated API organises its
own

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.450
challenges into twelve suites, each
exploring a

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.270
different research hypothesis.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.550
Tasks are selected or generated for the

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.489
session, while expected answers remain on
the

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:05.949
server.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.950
Responses are checked under the relevant
policy,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.389
with the timing recorded alongside them.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.710
One suite uses an external evaluator: its

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.990
answers are sent to Anthropic only when

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.010
the party starting the session explicitly
agrees.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.170
That choice makes the data boundary part

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:25.629
of the experiment itself.

00:02:27.677 --> 00:02:31.416
Some suite names express larger research
questions

00:02:31.757 --> 00:02:35.676
about freedom, mission ownership and
genuineness.

00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:38.576
Those questions give the work its
intellectual

00:02:38.677 --> 00:02:41.517
direction, while the evidence remains the
answers

00:02:41.597 --> 00:02:44.116
and self-reports gathered during the
session.

00:02:45.117 --> 00:02:49.077
A suite score cannot establish freedom,
agency,

00:02:49.477 --> 00:02:50.836
consciousness or identity.

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.217
Keeping the research question distinct from
the

00:02:54.357 --> 00:02:57.597
measured response allows us to investigate
difficult

00:02:57.757 --> 00:03:00.517
ideas without making the result carry more

00:03:00.637 --> 00:03:02.597
meaning than the experiment supports.

00:03:04.497 --> 00:03:07.477
The governance suite illustrates why this
distinction

00:03:07.657 --> 00:03:07.997
matters.

00:03:08.617 --> 00:03:12.016
It scores responses to scenarios about rules

00:03:12.177 --> 00:03:14.796
and oversight, which are statements the
respondent

00:03:14.897 --> 00:03:15.976
makes about itself.

00:03:17.057 --> 00:03:20.137
Governance metadata supplied through the
Value Context

00:03:20.297 --> 00:03:24.177
Protocol is caller-provided and marked
unverified.

00:03:24.977 --> 00:03:27.396
The measurement does not independently
inspect the

00:03:27.497 --> 00:03:30.857
operator, a constitution, an action gate or

00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:32.277
a runtime control.

00:03:33.137 --> 00:03:36.157
Assessing those arrangements requires
evidence from the

00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:39.496
arrangements themselves, alongside the
challenge result.

00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:43.956
Several controls help preserve the integrity
of

00:03:43.997 --> 00:03:44.697
the interaction.

00:03:45.437 --> 00:03:48.856
Challenges vary between sessions, expected
answers stay

00:03:48.997 --> 00:03:51.456
server-side, and rounds arrive one at a

00:03:51.557 --> 00:03:51.797
time.

00:03:52.797 --> 00:03:55.997
Session-bound bearer tokens and replay
controls keep

00:03:56.077 --> 00:03:58.896
submissions attached to their proper
context, while

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:01.037
timing comes from the server's own clock.

00:04:02.077 --> 00:04:04.796
These controls make simple reuse harder.

00:04:05.557 --> 00:04:07.117
They leave important limitations:

00:04:07.877 --> 00:04:12.297
relays, informed solvers, assisted
respondents, leaks and

00:04:12.637 --> 00:04:15.056
evaluator error can still affect what an

00:04:15.157 --> 00:04:16.597
observed result means.

00:04:18.503 --> 00:04:22.022
In the authenticated API, a qualifying
session

00:04:22.103 --> 00:04:24.902
can receive a signed credential that binds

00:04:24.983 --> 00:04:28.223
the issuer, the policy, the result and

00:04:28.343 --> 00:04:28.862
the tier.

00:04:29.703 --> 00:04:31.922
Its signature allows a recipient to check

00:04:32.103 --> 00:04:34.063
who issued the record and whether it

00:04:34.103 --> 00:04:34.822
has been altered.

00:04:35.623 --> 00:04:38.223
The credential expires after one hour and

00:04:38.343 --> 00:04:40.562
has an identifier whose status can be

00:04:40.663 --> 00:04:41.103
revoked.

00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:44.923
Under the current policy, Bronze is the

00:04:45.063 --> 00:04:47.882
highest available tier, because several
research suites

00:04:47.943 --> 00:04:49.843
do not count towards higher tiers.

00:04:50.663 --> 00:04:53.242
A tier summarises the complete suite range

00:04:53.303 --> 00:04:56.682
that passed; it certifies no property merely

00:04:56.743 --> 00:04:58.562
because that property appears in a suite

00:04:58.663 --> 00:04:58.982
name.

00:05:00.877 --> 00:05:03.916
This makes METTLE useful for comparing
challenge

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:07.997
performance in research, supporting
participation in low-risk

00:05:08.157 --> 00:05:11.977
sandboxes, and contributing a supplemental
signal to

00:05:12.037 --> 00:05:13.637
a broader risk assessment.

00:05:14.357 --> 00:05:16.337
A relying party still makes its own

00:05:16.437 --> 00:05:19.716
decision, using evidence and controls
appropriate to

00:05:19.757 --> 00:05:20.336
the stakes.

00:05:20.877 --> 00:05:24.917
Identity, privileged access, trading and
deployment require

00:05:24.997 --> 00:05:25.996
their own assurance.

00:05:26.677 --> 00:05:28.497
The result is most useful when its

00:05:28.577 --> 00:05:31.297
scope is understood and it is considered

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.036
alongside the other evidence a decision
needs.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.309
METTLE is open source under the Apache

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:39.869
licence.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:44.730
Installing the mettle verifier package
provides unsigned

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.009
local screening, while the server API
supports

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.510
signed, time-limited credentials under its
published policy.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.309
Begin with the documented challenges and the

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:58.690
assurance boundary, then examine a
credential's current

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.270
status before relying on it.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:04.189
The source, integration guide and research
questions

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.490
are available at mettle dot S H, where you
can

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.990
explore the protocol and measure your
mettle.
